          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "jusque is built on Latin ūsque \"all the way\" (Lewis & Short) with inde (EtymDB) or, in another view, dē; alors joins à and lors, which EtymDB traces to Latin illā hōrā \"at that hour\"."
            }
          ]
